  "_note": "Two kinds live here and they are NOT interchangeable. `raw_*` entries are the DATA LAYER's output: raw broker state, no reservations, per A2 (b) \u2014 the data layer is a dumb honest reporter. `composed_*` entries are the GOVERNOR's composed view: the same raw state plus reservations and activity the governor derives from the provenance ledger. The governor requires a composed view; handing it a raw one is a caller error, not a rejection (see README). `equity` (PROPOSED, added 2026-09-02) is the account's TOTAL equity, which a cap stated as a fraction of equity resolves against; it is set equal to `cash` in every fixture here so the arithmetic stays doable in the head. `ledger.open_risk` (PROPOSED, same date) is the ledger-derived risk already on the book: `total` is the sum of the GOVERNOR'S OWN computed max loss over every position bearing risk, `unpriced_positions` counts the covered calls that have no standalone max-loss figure (2e) and are therefore not in the total. It is zero in every pre-existing fixture \u2014 those accounts hold no priced risk \u2014 and saturated in `composed_open_risk_saturated`, which exists to fail x_total_open_risk.",
